artifact "Board Type Grid"

scene
  size: 1280 720
  background: #ffffff

widget layout.board
  title: "16:9 board · type grid"
  caption: "12 guides · body fills 3 readable measures"
  body: "The author turns on typeGrid and names how many guides to paint. The compiler keeps the 12-column skeleton for alignment, then pours this paragraph into three readable measures so a coding agent does not write a y for every line. 栏是度量，格子是参考：十二栏参考线仍在，正文按可读栏宽从 type0 流到下一栏，不靠作者手摆分栏坐标。This is still not InDesign — no running header, no jump folio, no optical kerning — but the same primitive that hops a page knife now fills type columns top to bottom, then left to right."
  typeGrid: true
  typeGridStep: 8
  typeGridCols: 12
  guides: true
